# Keep the build context minimal. The Dockerfile copies the root manifests by name and the
# whole packages/ folder, and anything that reaches the build stage is in the image's
# history for good: deleting it in a later layer does NOT remove it. A pattern here is
# anchored at the context root unless it starts with **/, which is why every rule below
# does. The first version of this file listed `dist`, `node_modules` and `session.json`
# bare, so they matched only at the root, and the host's build output and node_modules
# under packages/ went into the image (found by the 2026-09-23 audit).
#
# No exceptions, not even for folders that only exist at the root: `**/` also matches at
# the root, and test/dockerignore.test.js fails on any rule that does not start with it.
**/.git
**/.claude
**/docs
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.har
**/*.env
**/.env*
**/session.json
**/config.json
**/cookies.*
**/Care*Album*Photos/
**/Brightwheel*Photos/
**/.care-album-saver-production
